  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Independent media as the basis of a strong civil society and a key to developing democratic institutions.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&apos;s main idea is to increase access to quality content on situation in Ukraine for Ukrainian and foreign audiences. This includes reforms, human rights violations, ongoing war, war crimes and post-war recovery. Another important aspect is the collection and verification of information necessary to further the potential prosecution process of all those responsible for violating human rights and committing war crimes (including the collection of materials and evidence for a potential tribunal for Russian war criminals). Hromadske also wants to strengthen its potential as an NGO, stimulating civic engagement and searching for more innovative ways to interact with our audience. Thus, the organisation wants to increase the level of engagement of civil society representatives in the process of law and decision-making, thereby strengthening democratic institutions in the country.</narrative>
  </description>
